name w1-01-merge-1
timeout 300

# CAMPAIGN W1, SORTIE 1 OF 10 - RED FLAG / NELLIS: THE NEUTRAL MERGE, RUNG 1 OF THE LADDER.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w1-red-flag.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it is rung 1, and it is the geometry the doctrine sweep of the saturation gate is
# flown on (doc/doctrine-evolution.md section 4.2, S2).
#
# THE ANCHOR, AND IT IS [T1] SINCE THIS ROUND. The 414th Combat Training Squadron's own fact sheet was
# HTTP 403 to automated retrieval on every previous pass and is READ here through the Wayback Machine's
# capture of the identical URL (20240116184035, "current as of October 2022") - the same path that lifted
# O2's two CIA documents. It says, verbatim: "Lessons from Vietnam showed that if a pilot survived his
# first 10 combat missions, his probability of survival for remaining missions increased substantially.
# Red Flag was designed to expose each 'Blue' force pilot to their first 10 'combat missions' here at
# Nellis." THE TEN MISSIONS OF THIS CAMPAIGN ARE THEREFORE THE ANCHOR'S OWN NUMBER, not a [SET] choice,
# and the aggressors' job of providing "a scalable threat presentation to Blue forces which aids in
# achieving the desired learning outcomes for each mission" is the LADDER at [T1]. What the fact sheet
# does NOT say is anything about package sizes: it gives cumulative totals since 1975 (30,268 aircraft,
# 423,248 sorties) and no air tasking order, so every force size in this campaign stays [SET].
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION - and W1 is the campaign where it runs backwards. At Nellis the
# "MiG-29" is an F-16 of the 64th Aggressor Squadron in an adversary scheme [T4]; here it is the REAL
# mig29 module, with the R-73, the KOLS and the helmet cue the aggressor jet never had. RED IS THEREFORE
# MATERIALLY STRONGER THAN THE HISTORICAL OPPOSING FORCE, so a Blue result that still goes well says
# something STRONGER than a Nellis debrief did, and one that goes badly says nothing about the 64th.
# NO CATALOGUE ROW IS FLOWN IN ANY OF THE TEN FILES: A15 forbids an ALPHA row from answering a campaign
# question and every aggressor here is the mig29 module, which needs no generated deck.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET] inside the spec's own NTTR box (37.0-37.6 N,
# 115.5-116.6 W [T4], "approximate, verify against DEM"): one east-west lane at 37.30 N from -116.58
# (the aggressors' entry) to -115.52 (Blue's, the Nellis side). The lane is 93.9 km long, which is the
# arena's single most important property and is measured rather than assumed: the APG-68's own gate
# against a Fulcrum-sized target is 40 nm x (4.0/1.2)^0.25 = 100.0 km (doc/duels.md Knowledge 1), so THE
# RANGE IS SHORTER THAN BLUE'S RADAR REACH and no Blue jet on this arena ever flies a search phase it
# was not given. The N019's gate against an F-16 is 50.0 km, i.e. 53 % of the lane.
# GROUND: `--elev const`, so the range floor is 0 m and every altitude in this file is a height above
# THAT plane, not a chart ASL figure (the real NTTR floor is ~1.2-1.5 km; C4 means there is no terrain
# to mask anything anyway). Passing `--elev const` explicitly is a precondition and not a convention:
# fb-gym's own default is `swiss` whenever the baked DEM is on disk, and it validates a declared spawn
# altitude against the resolved ground (O3's warning, doc/campaigns/INDEX.md).
#
# THE GROUND TARGET, and campaign rule 3. `nvpit1` is a mock vehicle convoy on the range floor under the
# merge - one of the target kinds the fact sheet names by hand ("mock airfields, vehicle convoys, tanks,
# parked aircraft, bunkered defensive positions, missile sites" [T1]). IT IS NOT ATTACKED IN THIS FILE
# AND THAT IS A CAPABILITY STATEMENT, not an omission: `set task` selects ONE phase at spawn and
# pilot/FBPilot has no Bfm -> Attack transition at all (the only transitions out of a combat phase are
# Attack -> Route after the egress, FBPilot.cpp:1236/1245), so the spec's "post-fight Mk-82 pass" cannot
# be flown by the jet that fought the merge. Strafing it instead is blocked by C11 (gun bundles are not
# resolved against ground targets). The convoy is here for the reason rule 3 gives - it is why the fight
# is over this piece of desert - and the range gunnery half of the spec's rung 1 is not in the record.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: does the pilot convert a NEUTRAL merge into a firing position on the first
# pass, and what happens to the fight afterwards?
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG ISOLATES: close combat with nothing else in the file - one aircraft a side, no BVR
# phase, no flight, no datalink, both inside every launch zone either side owns from t = 0.
#
# THE `wp` LINE ON A BFM JET IS NOT DECORATION, AND THIS FILE IS WHERE THE CAMPAIGN FOUND OUT. Every
# combat unit in all ten W1 files carries one, because `modules/f16/FBF16FireControl.cpp:141` invalidates
# the WHOLE fire-control block when `state.Nav` is unreadable, and `systems/FBNavSystem` publishes
# nothing at all without a steerpoint (FBNavSystem.cpp:53, `if (Have || HaveBull)`). MEASURED on the
# first cut of this very file, which was written without one: `blk_firecontrol` = 0 for all 3,001 rows,
# `gun_sol_err` = -1 throughout, 0 `pilot BFM_SHOT` lines, 0 rounds fired, exit 3 with both jets alive
# and 14.8 s of unbroken lock at ranges from 7.5 km down to 185 m. Adding one `wp` line per jet and
# changing nothing else: exit 0, Blue's AIM-9 away at t = 1.0 s. The gate is silent - no rejection, no
# log line, and the only witness is a telemetry column nobody reads in a dogfight.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, `--elev const`, campaign step 1 AND standalone - fingerprint 3555795c02ef346f,
# identical both ways): exit 0, and the merge is DECIDED IN 10.1 SECONDS.
#   detection    Blue RADAR_CONTACT + LOCK at t = 1.0/1.1 s (4.04 nm); the aggressor 2.0 s later
#                (3.51 nm), and the 2.0 s is the F-16 spawning in `acm_hud` while the MiG's pilot must
#                switch the N019 to ACM over the command bus - doc/duels.md row 8's mechanism, on a
#                second arena
#   shots        Blue `pilot BFM_SHOT` t = 1.0 s at 7,483 m (Raero 12,000, cue +-30 deg); the aggressor
#                t = 3.0 s at 6,503 m (Raero 20,000, cue +-60 deg). NEITHER FIRES A ROUND FROM THE GUN
#                in the whole run (`gun_fired` 0 on both)
#   arrivals     AIM-9 at **1.819 m** -> `damage KILL` on the aggressor at t = 10.1 s (failed=4090).
#                R-73 at **2.622 m** 1.1 s later -> Blue DEGRADED and combat-effective (failed=4016)
#   the two radii are the reason and they are catalogue numbers: 2.32 m for the AIM-9M against this
#   airframe, 2.08 m for the R-73 (doc/duels.md row 9). duel-merge measured the R-73 at 2.64 m and the
#   same survival; W1 reproduces it at 2.622 m, i.e. to 0.02 m, over a different piece of the planet
#   lock retention  15.1 s (Blue) and 7.1 s (the aggressor) out of 67.8 s of engagement
#   the convoy   `mission UNIT_RESULT unit=nvpit1 result=INTACT`
# SO THE ANSWER IS YES, ON THE FIRST PASS AND WITH THE ROUND ON THE RAIL. What this file does NOT measure
# is a turning fight: doc/pilot.md 2.9 still holds and neither ACM box re-acquires after a pass.
#
# WHAT TO READ: `stores DETONATION missM` beside each round's own `fuzeM` (2.32 m for the AIM-9M against
# this airframe, 2.08 m for the R-73 - doc/duels.md row 9), `eng_shot_s` on both jets, and `bfm_rng`
# for the seconds each pilot held the other at all.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 is a decided merge and a real verdict; exit 3 with both alive is the
# re-acquisition gap of doc/pilot.md 2.9 and is a RESULT, not noise. exit 2 - a physical K.O. of a
# healthy jet - would be a defect.

unit rf1blu
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 37.30000 -116.05500 5000 270.0 380    # 8.0 km apart, co-altitude, head-on: duel-merge's geometry
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off                            # a merge is fought on own sensors (doc/missions/combat.md)
  set fcr_mode acm_hud                        # the auto-lock box: no thumb needed
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set gun_rounds 510
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 37.30000 -116.30000 5000 380              # the briefed range run: on WEST through the aggressors' end
  objective kill unit rf1agr
  objective survive

unit rf1agr
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 37.30000 -116.14500 5000 90.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad                           # the BFM pilot switches it to ACM in the fight himself
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set kols_mode ir_cc                         # the close-combat infrared field, +-15 deg, auto-track
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r73
  set store 4 r73
  set gun_rounds 150
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 37.30000 -115.90000 5000 380              # ...and the aggressor's, on EAST through Blue's
  objective kill unit rf1blu
  objective survive

unit nvpit1
  module target_soft                          # mock vehicle convoy on the range floor [T1 target kind]
  team hostile
  spawn 37.30000 -116.10000 ground 90.0 0
